@bio:

David J Smith was professor of music at Northumbria
University, where he led an AHRC-funded project on ‘Digital
directions for collected editions’ (2021–23) and co-edited
a special issue of <i>Journal of New Music Research</i> on ‘The
future of scholarly, critical editions of music’. He has
produced scholarly, critical editions of music by Peter
Philips (c.1560–1628) and Richard Dering (c.1580–1630) for
Musica Britannica and is currently working with Andrew
Woolley on the keyboard music of Henry Purcell
(c.1659–1695) for The Purcell Society Edition. 

@@END: BIO